  "description": "Exposure Frameset\n\nTHE LATEST EVOLUTION OF OUR UNIQUE MASON EXPOSURE FRAMESET Our Italian-made Dedacciai steel bikepacking and adventure bicycle. Designed with larger clearances and more relaxed geometry, the Exposure is highly adaptable with multiple load and accessory-carrying configurations. Masterpiece is a pretty big word to throw into a bike review, but I’m as comfortable and excited about using it here. – Bike Perfect 2023 This lovingly crafted frameset is developed for fast, long-distance, extended adventure touring over very variable and unpredictable terrain. It's designed with frame clearance for 650b x 58mm [2.25”] and 700c x 55mm tyres. The Exposure's custom-shaped, progressively butted, phosphate-coated Dedacciai Zero Uno tubeset is engineered by Dedacciai for long range riding, with class-leading toughness and weight, combined with engaging pedalling feel, ride quality and efficiency. The Reynolds 631 44mm head tube is CNC-machined by Bear exclusively for the Exposure. A recent update brings MASON-designed CNC-machined dropouts to the Exposure, compatible with the Universal Derailleur Hanger standard. This frame is paired with a MASON full-carbon fork – the RangeFinder AS ['AS' for AdventureSport] - which is tuned for all surface riding conditions. The Rangefinder AS features a full set of moulded-in eyelets, and is designed to be fitted with a front rack or rando-style bag support, along with accessory cages and internally routed dynamo light. SUPPORT & SAFETY DOCUMENTS Riding Conditions Guide | Exposure Framesheet | Initial Setup & Care Guide | Bicycle Owner's Manual | Rack & Carrier Safety\n\n100% Italian TIG-welded/silver-brazed frame manufacturing, wet-painting, and finishing.\n\nFrame clearance with capacity for 650b x 58mm [2.25”] and 700c x 55mm tyres. [700c x 45mm approx. including mudguards]\n\nCOLOURS AVAILABLE: FilterYellow. OpticGreen. AccursedOchre. DiffuserBlack Metallic.\n\nInternal gear and brake routing as standard. Exit for Di2/EPS cable on seat tube with stainless steel reinforcement\n\nDiscreet internal dynamo-light top tube routing with stainless steel port reinforcement\n\nBottle/accessory cage boss placements as standard: 4 down tube (top side); 3 down tube (underneath); 3 seat tube; 2 top tube, 2 seat stays (both sides)\n\nUK-made 44mm head tube machined by Bear from Reynolds 631 steel for a semi-integrated headset.\n\nClearance for 48/31T double chainset | 40T single chainring.\n\nChain pip neatly holds the chain on the chainring whilst the wheel is removed for travelling.",
